# `/* x /* y */ z */` - Swift block comments nest, and that is why the
# construct needs a hand at all rather than a regex.
#
# A non-nesting reader closes at the first `*/`, byte 21, and then meets
# `z */` as code. Only a hand carrying a depth counter reaches [10, 27),
# which is exactly the state a stateless implementation does not keep.
#
# This and its sibling are the only falsifiers the row has: with the row
# un-seated (`aud-r3`) both fall 4/4 -> 2/4 on `holds multiline_comment`,
# while every corpus board arm reads the row at exactly zero because
# `Chunked.swift` has no `/*`. A pair sweep once called it inert on that
# evidence; `research/joinery/consort/RESULT-2-swift.md`.
roots 1
mends 0
holds multiline_comment
spans multiline_comment 10 27
